{"id":"b10","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":12,"of":22,"title":"Exactly two","titleHe":"זוּגִי","goal":"Use the dual ending ־ַיִם, and stop saying two years the long way.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew has a third number between singular and plural, kept for pairs: the dual. It is one ending, ־ַיִם, and it does the work of the number two, so the number itself is left out."},{"type":"table","caption":"Time, in twos","head":["one","two"],"rows":[["יוֹם — a day","יוֹמַיִם — two days"],["שָׁבוּעַ — a week","שְׁבוּעַיִם — two weeks"],["חֹדֶשׁ — a month","חָדְשַׁיִם — two months"],["שָׁנָה — a year","שְׁנָתַיִם — two years"],["שָׁעָה — an hour","שַׁעֲתַיִם — two hours"],["פַּעַם — once","פַּעֲמַיִם — twice"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"These are not optional. שְׁתֵּי שָׁנִים is understood but reads as a mistake; שְׁנָתַיִם is what a speaker says and what a book prints."},{"type":"text","body":"The same ending sits permanently on things that come in pairs — and there it is simply the plural, not a count of two: יָדַיִם hands, רַגְלַיִם feet, עֵינַיִם eyes, אָזְנַיִם ears, שִׁנַּיִם teeth. So do the objects built to match them: מִשְׁקָפַיִם glasses, מִכְנָסַיִם trousers, נַעֲלַיִם shoes, אוֹפַנַּיִם a bicycle."},{"type":"text","body":"When you do want to put a number in front of a noun, two has its own short form: שְׁנֵי before a masculine noun, שְׁתֵּי before a feminine one."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"שְׁנֵי סְפָרִים","en":"two books"},{"he":"שְׁתֵּי בָּנוֹת","en":"two daughters"},{"he":"גַּרְתִּי שָׁם שְׁנָתַיִם.","en":"I lived there for two years."},{"he":"לָמַדְתִּי שַׁעֲתַיִם.","en":"I studied for two hours."}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Two hundred and two thousand are duals too: מָאתַיִם and אַלְפַּיִם. If you ever wondered why they look nothing like the other round numbers, that is why."}],"vocab":[{"he":"יוֹמַיִם","en":"two days","translit":"yomayim"},{"he":"שְׁבוּעַיִם","en":"two weeks","translit":"shvu'ayim"},{"he":"חָדְשַׁיִם","en":"two months","translit":"chodshayim"},{"he":"שְׁנָתַיִם","en":"two years","translit":"shnatayim"},{"he":"שַׁעֲתַיִם","en":"two hours","translit":"sha'atayim"},{"he":"אַלְפַּיִם","en":"two thousand","translit":"alpayim"},{"he":"שְׁנֵי","en":"two (before a m. noun)","translit":"shnei"},{"he":"שְׁתֵּי","en":"two (before a f. noun)","translit":"shtei"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["door","two days","parents","children"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יוֹמַיִם","translit":"yomayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["fever, heat","soul, self, person","goat","two weeks"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שְׁבוּעַיִם","translit":"shvu'ayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["already","a city wall","beautiful","two months"],"correct":3,"prompt":"חָדְשַׁיִם","translit":"chodshayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["sad","two years","Sabbath loaf","seems, looks"],"correct":1,"prompt":"שְׁנָתַיִם","translit":"shnatayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["season","begins","two hours","ability"],"correct":2,"prompt":"שַׁעֲתַיִם","translit":"sha'atayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["two thousand","vision","a tribe — also a rod","midrash, exposition"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אַלְפַּיִם","translit":"alpayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["restaurant","autumn","thing, word","two (before a m. noun)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שְׁנֵי","translit":"shnei"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “two months”?","options":["רַע","כִּמְעַט","חָדְשַׁיִם","מָלוֹן"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “two years”?","options":["שְׁנָתַיִם","בֵּן","יְשׁוּעָה","מְאֹד"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["אַלְפַּיִם","שַׁעֲתַיִם","שְׁנָתַיִם","שְׁתֵּי"],"correct":3,"say":"שְׁתֵּי","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “two weeks”?","options":["שְׁבוּעַיִם","מֵאָז","סְתָו","בִּלְתִּי"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"שְׁתֵּי","translit":"shtei","en":"two (before a f. noun)"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “two (before a f. noun)”?","options":["שְׁתֵּי","עָשִׁיר","וָו","מֶרְחָק"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"גַּרְתִּי שָׁם ___.","en":"I lived there for two years.","options":["שְׁנָתַיִם","שְׁבוּעַיִם","אַלְפַּיִם","שְׁתֵּי"],"correct":0,"full":"גַּרְתִּי שָׁם שְׁנָתַיִם."},{"type":"match","pairs":[["יוֹמַיִם","two days"],["שְׁבוּעַיִם","two weeks"],["חָדְשַׁיִם","two months"],["שְׁנָתַיִם","two years"],["שַׁעֲתַיִם","two hours"]]},{"type":"type","q":"Write “two months” in Hebrew","answer":"חָדְשַׁיִם","hint":"chodshayim"}]}